      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect there is a configuration issue here, possibly with the [CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX](http://cs/h/chromium/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/include/config_chip.h?l\u003d971) flag. I ran an experiment by adding `#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e` to `system.h` and got the same compilation error. I then replaced that with the following and the compilation error went away.\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX\n#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e\n#endif\n```\n\nI don\u0027t know if this is the correct solution but it is at least a clue. \n\nNote: There are [other places](http://source/search?q\u003dunistd.h%20f:platform%2Fec%2F\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fchromium%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch%2F%2B%2Fmain) where `unistd.h` is included so digging into the config files of builds using them will likely be helpful.",
