      "message": "Sorry for the brief comment on my previous response, I wasn\u0027t at my computer and only had a minute or so and wasn\u0027t able to get back online after.\n\n## Context\n\nTo provide context, I ran my tests on top of a clean checkout of `cros/main` at commit [e1cfeb867c](go/crrv/e1cfeb867cc7c8a853198ceff80c375051598f60) (from go/cl-c/4068487).\n\n## Baseline test\n\nI added `#include \u003cunisted.h\u003e` to `include/system.h` to see if I would see the same failure you described. Here is a diff that shows the changes:\n```\ndiff --git a/include/system.h b/include/system.h\nindex c7884199e1..47df96e4a8 100644\n--- a/include/system.h\n+++ b/include/system.h\n@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@\n #ifndef __CROS_EC_SYSTEM_H\n #define __CROS_EC_SYSTEM_H\n \n+#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e\n+\n #include \"atomic.h\"\n #include \"common.h\"\n #include \"compile_time_macros.h\"\n```\n\nI received the same `unistd.h: No such file or directory` error that you were describing:\n```\nbobbycasey@bobby:~/chromiumos/src/platform/ec$ c zmake build herobrine \nToolchain \u003czmake.toolchains.CorebootSdkToolchain object at 0x7efc4bd08d68\u003e selected by probe function.\nBuilding herobrine in /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine.\nSkip reconfiguring herobrine:rw due to previous cmake run of equivalent configuration.  Run with --clobber if this optimization is undesired.\nSkip reconfiguring herobrine:ro due to previous cmake run of equivalent configuration.  Run with --clobber if this optimization is undesired.\nBuilding herobrine:ro: /usr/bin/ninja -C /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/build-ro\nBuilding herobrine:rw: /usr/bin/ninja -C /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/build-rw\nFAILED: modules/ec/zephyr/CMakeFiles/ec_shim.dir/shim/chip/npcx/system.c.obj \nFAILED: modules/ec/zephyr/CMakeFiles/ec_shim.dir/shim/chip/npcx/system.c.obj \nIn file included from /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/chip/npcx/system.c:6:\nIn file included from /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/chip/npcx/system.c:6:\n../modules/ec/include/system.h:11:10: fatal error: unistd.h: No such file or directory\n../modules/ec/include/system.h:11:10: fatal error: unistd.h: No such file or directory\n   11 | #include \u003cunistd.h\u003e\n   11 | #include \u003cunistd.h\u003e\n      |          ^~~~~~~~~~\n      |          ^~~~~~~~~~\ncompilation terminated.\n...\n```\n\n## Test with CONFIG flags\nNow that the baseline test showing the same failure I tried conditionally including `unistd.h` based on `CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX` using the following diff:\n```\nbobbycasey@bobby:~/chromiumos/src/platform/ec$ git diff\ndiff --git a/include/system.h b/include/system.h\nindex c7884199e1..c2a2bfbb92 100644\n--- a/include/system.h\n+++ b/include/system.h\n@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@\n #ifndef __CROS_EC_SYSTEM_H\n #define __CROS_EC_SYSTEM_H\n \n+#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_POSIX\n+#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e\n+#endif\n+\n #include \"atomic.h\"\n #include \"common.h\"\n #include \"compile_time_macros.h\"\n```\n\nWith the conditional include block in place the build succeeded. \n```\nbobbycasey@bobby:~/chromiumos/src/platform/ec$ c zmake build herobrine \nToolchain \u003czmake.toolchains.CorebootSdkToolchain object at 0x7fc8a2eef908\u003e selected by probe function.\nBuilding herobrine in /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine.\nSkip reconfiguring herobrine:ro due to previous cmake run of equivalent configuration.  Run with --clobber if this optimization is undesired.\nSkip reconfiguring herobrine:rw due to previous cmake run of equivalent configuration.  Run with --clobber if this optimization is undesired.\nBuilding herobrine:ro: /usr/bin/ninja -C /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/build-ro\nBuilding herobrine:rw: /usr/bin/ninja -C /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/build-rw\nINFO:root:Zephyr Base: /mnt/host/source/src/third_party/zephyr/main\nINFO:root:Zephyr Base: /mnt/host/source/src/third_party/zephyr/main\nINFO:root:Including modules: [/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/hal_stm32, /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/cmsis, /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/ec, /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/nanopb]\nINFO:root:Including modules: [/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/hal_stm32, /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/cmsis, /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/ec, /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/nanopb]\nINFO:root:Version string: Zephyr-Kernel_v3.2.104620-ec:e1cfeb,os:233b56,cmsis:4aa3ff,hal_stm32:adc1ea,nanopb:0cdcea\nINFO:root:Version string: Zephyr-Kernel_v3.2.104620-ec:e1cfeb,os:233b56,cmsis:4aa3ff,hal_stm32:adc1ea,nanopb:0cdcea\nINFO:root:Writing header to /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/build-ro/modules/ec/zephyr/include/ec_version.h\nINFO:root:Writing header to /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/build-rw/modules/ec/zephyr/include/ec_version.h\nMemory region         Used Size  Region Size  %age Used\nMemory region         Used Size  Region Size  %age Used\n           FLASH:      245360 B       256 KB     93.60%\n           FLASH:      245360 B       256 KB     93.60%\n             RAM:       48728 B        64 KB     74.35%\n             RAM:       48728 B        64 KB     74.35%\n        IDT_LIST:          0 GB         2 KB      0.00%\n        IDT_LIST:          0 GB         2 KB      0.00%\n```\n\nI have also run `$ c zmake build -a` with this patch in place and did not observe any compilation errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nAs noted in my previous comment, I am not sure if this is the correct solution but I was able to replicate the failure by including `unistd.h` and then successfully compile using the conditional blocks. This does not appear to cause any build issues and, while I have not performed any testing on the builds, I suspect doing a build comparison would yield no changes between the unpatched and patched versions.",
