      "message": "Sorry for multiple comments, but I meant to include some references to what led me down the path of considering configurations. First, I looked around moma for references to Zephyr and `unistd.h` and found go/cl-c/4047098, which wasn\u0027t completely related but did show files that include `unistd.h` being modified and tested in a Zephyr context. This led me to believe that the file must exist somewhere in the build chain and got me considering build time configurations. \n\nI then found [Zephyr issue #6719](http://go/gh/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/issues/6719) which seems to be complaining of a similar issue and pointed to a potential conflict between the `posix/unistd.h` and `unistd.h`. That issue was resolved in go/gh/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/6820 and the comments recommend using `#include \u003cunistd.h\u003e` over `#include \u003cposix/unistd.h\u003e`. There is also some discussion in the review about potential interactions between the POSIX config and the NEWLIB config so we should be careful, deliberate, and consistent about which `sleep` implementation are using.",
